# Line endings for the GENERATED launchers (field report 2026-08-07, defect 2).
#
# This file is tracked, so the installer's `git ls-files` copy carries it into every brain
# it creates — which is where it does its work: the brain commits its own launch.cmd /
# launch.sh, and `rehydrate.mjs` does not regenerate them on a second machine. Without a
# stated rule, a clone gets whatever the machine's core.autocrlf happens to be, and the
# generator's careful bytes are rewritten behind its back.
#
# The two families need OPPOSITE things, which is exactly how one rule ends up wrongly
# applied to both:
#
#   .cmd — cmd.exe re-seeks a batch file BY BYTE OFFSET as it runs. With LF-only endings
#          the accounting drifts and it resumes MID-TOKEN: the field stderr showed `REM`
#          executed as 'M', plus 'lf-heal' and 'epends', fragments of our own comments.
#
#   .sh  — sh treats a trailing CR as part of the token, so a CRLF launcher dies on an
#          invisible byte with an unreadable "command not found".
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf
